{"ok":true,"result":{"id":"request-13","jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"content":[{"text":"<instruction>\n---\nname: sg-private\ndescription: Private path, URL, and Vivaldi bookmark memory with explicit persistence and public/private isolation.\n---\n\n# sg-private\n\n## Mission\n\n`sg-private` is the public owner for explicit private requests: machine-local pointer memory, Vivaldi bookmarks, and bounded access to declared durable private-data namespaces.\n\n## Scope Gate\n\nResolve the intended private action and source, then load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`. Supplying a path, URL, file, bookmark, or private repository is not permission to persist or inspect it. Durable private-data access requires an explicit request and declared namespace.\n\n## Required References\n\nResolve `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT` through the shared canonical-path doctrine, verify the root and `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/603-sg-private/SKILL.md` exist, then load that canonical engine. If the root or file is missing, stop with a visible error; never fall back to a sibling runtime path. Execute it end to end; `603-sg-private` remains an expert/internal engine only.\n\n## Validation\n\nUse the runtime engine's synthetic proof and private/public boundary checks. Never place real paths, URLs, notes, bookmark results, private repository metadata, or backups in public Git evidence.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\nWhen persistence intent is absent, treat the supplied value as transient and continue the original task without memorizing it. Stop only when persistence was requested but the value may contain a credential or secret, the requested source is unclear in a way that changes retention, or access would exceed the named private source.\n\n## Report Modes\n\nLoad `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/reporting-contract.md` before reporting. Keep private values in the operator conversation only when needed and keep internal engine names out of user-facing reports.\n\n</instruction>","type":"text"}],"isError":false}}}
